<title>TAIWAN: First Int'l Jan sales up 25 percent.</title>
<headline>First Int'l Jan sales up 25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First International Computer Inc, Taiwan's second largest computer firm, said on Friday its January sales rose 25 percent to T$2.691 billion from the same month a year ago.</p>
<p>The statement did not give profit figures.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
